{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1288370-wold-newton","id":1288370,"title":"Wold Newton","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Trinity Continuum"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-02-15T13:00:58-08:00","id":1288370,"title":"Wold Newton","content":"In <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/contorting-your-continuum-trinity-continuum/\" target=\"_blank\">Contorting Your Continuum</a>, we have the following news report:<br /> <div style=\"margin-left:40px\"><span style=\"font-family:times New Roman\">December 13, 1795: EXTRAORDINARY STONE Falls from Atmosphere \u2013 Lands at Wold Newton Cottage. Proof of Existence of Extra-Terrestrial Matter?</span></div><br /> For those of you who aren't aware, this is a reference to the <a href=\"https://en.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wold_Newton_family\" target=\"_blank\">Wold Newton Family</a>, a literary concept that is used to tie together many Victorian-age adventurers such as Doc Savage, Tarzan, Sherlock Holmes, Phileus Fogg, the unnamed protagonist of H.G.Wells' <i>the Time Machine</i>, and many, many others. It appears that Ian is hinting that the Wold Newton event and its consequences are part of the Trinity Continuum: the meteorite that crashed in Wold Newton in 1795 serves as a sort of minor Hammersmith Event that sets off a Victorian Age era of adventurers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T13:07:27-08:00","id":1288372,"title":"","content":"Well... from the context of the post, it seems more it <i>could</i> be part of the Continuum, if desired","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T13:49:55-08:00","id":1288386,"title":"","content":"I think it\u2019s pretty obvious who the Old Man running the International Detective Agency and it\u2019s Irregulars in 1E Adventure! was.<br /> <br /> Though I like the idea of subverting expectations and revealing that its Dr. Watson (who replaces Arthur Conan Doyle in-setting alltogether, he became a popular author reporting on his real experiences with Holmes). Holmes was never actually seen again after he and Moriarty went over the falls, and Watson ended up making up more adventures to meet public demand and process his own grief.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":1098,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","user":"glamourweaver","date":". 02-15-2019, 06:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T14:09:03-08:00","id":1288390,"title":"","content":"Throw the Viscount Greystoke in as one of the Aeon Society\u2019s original wealthy patrons.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T15:30:16-08:00","id":1288415,"title":"","content":"I don't have much to add, except to say this is all very awesome.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T22:20:05-08:00","id":1288526,"title":"","content":"Right up my alley! So we now have another Hammersmith type event awesome!<br /> <br /> I do go with most of these characters exist, or I mix a few together, like Tarzan is cool and all but I think I like Kazar better. Hmm but what if Kevin Plundarr\u2019s family was related to Lord Greystokes or a rival family, or maybe I mix em together.<br /> <br /> But yes I definitely have events before the Hammersmith Incident, and days of limited Tech Miracles of Nature such as a meteorite works in a pinch!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T22:31:28-08:00","id":1288528,"title":"","content":"But I really love the Lesgue of Extraordinary Gentlemen, the concept is fun and Brilliant. So for my world I do a similar thing. basically Rip Van winkle is a kind of immortal whose immortality is supported by his slumbers. So he sleeps and wakes ups two or three times every Century, and whenever he wakes up he\u2019s compelled by fate to encounter 4 other heroes of the Era to stand against 5 of the greatest and most wicked of beings of the Era who seemed to also be brought together via serendipity. So Far I worked on an 1820ish, 1860ish, and 1930ish Group and threat. It\u2019s rather fun and I think I would like to reference it in my games and have them encountered in an historical game. I need to work on earlier time periods and later time Periods. I\u2019m thinking 1900\u2019s he wakes up with greater and greater Frequency.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m thinking he may be compelled to sleep if awake too long, maybe after a generation and then Sleeps for twenty years at least. Or Maybe also he is compelled to sleep when injured gravely as a rejuvenating Coma.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-15T22:41:54-08:00","id":1288530,"title":"","content":"The first eximorph of the modern era was created in Victor Frankenstein\u2019s lab and may still be living at the North Pole","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T01:34:30-08:00","id":1288546,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1288370-wold-newton?p=1288530#post1288530\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first eximorph of the modern era was created in Victor Frankenstein\u2019s lab and may still be living at the North Pole</div> </div> </div> </div>My God... Santa Claus...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T07:19:08-08:00","id":1288593,"title":"","content":"Actually, I was thinking that Wold Newton might explain Calvin Hammersmith.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T08:50:15-08:00","id":1288610,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dataweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/trinity/1288370-wold-newton?p=1288593#post1288593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Actually, I was thinking that Wold Newton might explain Calvin Hammersmith.</div> </div> </div> </div>That s a good explanation, but he would have to be over a hundred years old to be born just after the event. Not impossible for Novas/Psiads...<br /> <br /> Edit: ok, he could be a descendent if the family","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":24985,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","user":"Mateus Luz","date":". 02-16-2019, 11:57 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T08:57:54-08:00","id":1288613,"title":"","content":"It's the Wold Newton Family for a reason: it's a hereditary power passed down from the two carriages of people who were in the vicinity of the meteorite strike.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div style=\"margin-left:40px\"> <div align=\"center\">My hacks: <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwtrin\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#0000FF\">Trinity Continuum</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwscion\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008000\">Scion</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwExalt\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#DAA520\">Exalted</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwcwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#800000\">World of Darkness</span></a>, <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/dwnwod\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Chronicles of Darkness</span></a></div> </div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/421-dataweaver","name":"Dataweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T12:01:56-08:00","id":1288666,"title":"","content":"Yeah exactly it\u2019s the whole point is it\u2019s the descendants of those exposed.<br /> <br /> But I imagine in the Setting those pulp heroes aren\u2019t all related to the two families. I would have some of them related but I would keep it as an inaccurate theory, and the meteorite resonated beyond what was suspected.<br /> <br /> And we don\u2019t know what was up with Hammersmith. I mean can Nova tech produce Flux and Psi, I didn\u2019t think so. But I think maybe a Talent could make a device, and I think he was influenced by outside sources. In my Trinity Multiverse setting Hammersmith gathered a Think tank to brainstorm before he developed his Zero point engine. So he gathered a number of individuals like Mycroft and Tesla, and had a correspondence with Einstein. This would have included a young Doc Savage or maybe his parents.<br /> <br /> And the likes of<br /> Professor Craig Kennedy<br /> Dr. John Evelyn Thorndyke<br /> Lamont Cranston<br /> And Ulysses Paxton.<br /> <br /> But several of these individuals would have helped him Assemble a number of secret Journals like<br /> <br /> -Journals of Mars<br /> -journal of Victor Frankenstein<br /> -Journal of Blavatsky<br /> -Journal of Da Vinci<br /> -Journal of Merlin\u2019s Lost Apprentice<br /> -Journal of the Black Tulku<br /> <br /> With only Hammersmith having access to them all.<br /> <br /> In my Trinity Multiverse idea (three tied together Universes with a different Survivor of the Hammersmith Incident each, and a secret zero universe where no one survived) Hammersmith was secretly trying to become immortal with his Engine, and a lot of the Theories were a combination of what he discovered in Da Vinci\u2019s hidden Journal and Einsteins correspondence. And secretly Da Vinci has become immortal and lives in a secret Eternal City Between the Universes, and there are actually 3 Da Vinci\u2019s from three Earths.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T15:05:12-08:00","id":1288749,"title":"","content":"For some reason I can't help but think of the idea that after the meetings with Hammersmith, Einstein then later on coast of the US government and sees about establishing a city of scientists where they can research freely. In times such as town would be called Eureka and it would become quite important for human development. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <br /> <br /> Oh and I totally think that Jack Carter is a Talent! Hehe <br /> <br /> And now this somehow makes me wanting to think about how the Stargate Universe fits in and what sort of Inspired they are. Lol <br /> <br /> Sorry not sorry! <br /> <br /> Oh. By the way I really like the idea of the meteorites crash releasing energies that later on make more inspired. Those who write around the crash gained the most power, and so do The Descendants. But as the time goes on the energy of the meteorite spreads to hear the planet and helps other people become inspired with no ties to the original people.<br /> <br /> The one thing I will say is I wouldn't make this a active event. What I mean by that is I would not have there be people or species or dimensional Gods who put the asteroid meteor right onto the planet. It was either a chance or an after the event of something else going on. (I can't help it think of something like how Superman's planet sent out Kryptonite to Earth when it was destroyed. Maybe the meteorite is the shards of some sort of telluric planet.)<br /> <br /> And honestly for my love of pulp and adventure and all that I didn't know about this event. So I'm really glad that it was mentioned here cuz I looked it up and now I am quite fascinating.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/661-lordheru","name":"LordHeru","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar661_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1100"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T17:04:46-08:00","id":1288783,"title":"","content":"So many good memories about Eureka and the other SciFi Chanel series... Eureka fits so nice on TC it should be part of the setting, Eureka, the city of Talents? Their super science is extremely advanced, but not powers anyway, it\u2019s just a few decades ahead of the prototypes of the rest of the world...<br /> <br /> SG would not fit nicely to Trinity Continuum, but would be fun to use some of the concepts and aliens, mainly the Ancients and possible the SGs. The Ancients fit perfectly in the idea of \u201cafter 10k years of space they rise above matter\u201d, and the SG working as transport between the former worlds too. You find a part of one of the cities on BE to partially powered, maybe with a SG in the middle. Find out the species were already on a few different planets using their quantum tech to open wormholes around... what would the psions do? It\u2019s obviously quantum and obviously not aberrant...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481584/house-rules-bundle-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">House Rules - The Bundle</a> - House Rules for Everyone<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/481581/powered-inspiration-bundle\" target=\"_blank\">Powered Inspired</a> - Powered Characters using Inspiration and Gifts<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/413362/Fists-and-Tomes-BUNDLE\" target=\"_blank\">Fists and Tomes</a> - Inspired Martial Arts and Mysticism for Talents<br /> <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/en/product/492147/supertech\" target=\"_blank\">Supertech</a> - Super Science in the hands of Talents","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24985-mateus-luz","name":"Mateus Luz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24985_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2950"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T22:24:06-08:00","id":1288847,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah I have it The Journals of Mars were brough by Ulysses Paxton another human who went to Mars.<br /> <br /> I figure Mycroft was supremely useful for Hammersmith to bounce ideas off of, as well as help him connect the dots, Einstein and Da Vinci inspired him and Tesla helped him hammer out some of the hard science of energy.<br /> <br /> Perhaps the Meteor was something like the Bottle City of Kandor, so it was a miniature world, so it held a The Quantum of a whole Civilization within it that was released when it Crashed. Hell what if the meteor was land of Liliput! Gulliver travelled there and was shrunk in order to do so but even after shrinking he was still to massive.<br /> <br /> Or since most of the Woldon events involved Talents, the Meteor was a result of our Universe Colliding/Overlapping with another in a freak anomalous conversion. Hell this could explain the Meteor as a Tiny World, as maybe that Universe was of a tinier Scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-16T22:28:26-08:00","id":1288849,"title":"","content":"Also while Stargate has some interesting ideas I would steal, I would also totally think I could handle those ideas better when I reimagine them. Though I loved the Cinematic nature of the Movie, and Teal\u2019c and Macguyver.<br /> <br /> And yeah definitely a town called Eureka exists, and even before the Galatea explosion it had a lot of worlds supertech concentrated in an American town. Probably were a lot of the Talents super tech comes from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}